=== COMPILER2 DIAGNOSTICS ===
  [hir] E0010

  × invalid top-level `const`: a global variable binds a single name; destructuring and `_` are only available inside a body
    ╭─[declarations.baml:12:1]
 12 │ const [FIRST, SECOND] = [1, 2];
    · ───────────────┬───────────────
    ·                ╰── a global variable binds one name: `const NAME = value;` or `const NAME: Type = value;`
    ╰────

  [hir] E0010

  × invalid top-level `const`: a global variable binds a single name; destructuring and `_` are only available inside a body
    ╭─[declarations.baml:15:1]
 15 │ const _ = 3;
    · ──────┬─────
    ·       ╰── a global variable binds one name: `const NAME = value;` or `const NAME: Type = value;`
    ╰────

  [hir] E0010

  × invalid top-level `const`: only a type annotation may follow a global variable's name
    ╭─[declarations.baml:18:1]
 18 │ const ALIAS: let OTHER = 4;
    · ─────────────┬─────────────
    ·              ╰── a global variable binds one name: `const NAME = value;` or `const NAME: Type = value;`
    ╰────

  [hir] E0010

  × invalid top-level `const`: `const … else` needs a body to leave; a global variable's initializer must produce its value
    ╭─[declarations.baml:21:1]
 21 │ const MAYBE: int = 5 else { 6 };
    · ────────────────┬───────────────
    ·                 ╰── a global variable binds one name: `const NAME = value;` or `const NAME: Type = value;`
    ╰────

  [hir] E0176

  × `baml` cannot be used as a binding name: syntax such as `spawn` and `env.X` refers to the `baml` package, which this binding would hide. A class or function may still be named `baml`.
    ╭─[declarations.baml:24:7]
 24 │ const baml = 7;
    ·       ──┬─
    ·         ╰── reserved binding name
    ╰────

  [validation] E0011

  × name `Duplicated` defined 2 times as: let, function
    ╭─[declarations.baml:27:7]
 27 │ const Duplicated = 8;
    ·       ─────┬────
    ·            ╰── first defined as let here
    ╰────
    ╭─[declarations.baml:29:10]
 29 │ function Duplicated() -> int {
    ·          ─────┬────
    ·               ╰── duplicate function definition
    ╰────

  [type] E0002

  × unresolved type: NoSuchType
    ╭─[declarations.baml:34:19]
 34 │ const UNRESOLVED: NoSuchType = 10;
    ·                   ──────────
    ╰────

  [hir] E0147

  × the `_` wildcard type can only be inferred in a `let` binding or a `throws` clause, not in a global variable's type
    ╭─[declarations.baml:35:13]
 35 │ const HOLE: map<string, _> = { "eleven": 11 };
    ·             ───────┬──────
    ·                    ╰── `_` cannot be inferred here
    ╰────

  [hir] E0110

  × `void` can only be used as a function return type, not as a let binding annotation
    ╭─[declarations.baml:36:16]
 36 │ const NOTHING: void = null;
    ·                ──┬─
    ·                  ╰── `void` not allowed here
    ╰────

  [type] E0001

  × mismatched types
    ╭─[declarations.baml:39:28]
 39 │ const MISMATCHED: string = 12;
    ·                            ─┬
    ·                             ╰── expected `string`, found `12`
    ╰────

  [hir] E0010

  × global variables are declared with `const`: `const NAME = value;`
    ╭─[declarations.baml:43:1]
 43 │ let WITH_LET = 13;
    · ─┬─
    ·  ╰── write `const` here; `let` is only allowed inside a body
    ╰────
